  "summary": "Coven is a documented Rust agent-orchestration platform connecting Claude-powered agents to a Go gateway over bidirectional gRPC, with CLI/TUI/HTTP/Matrix frontends, pluggable LLM backends, and modular tool packs. Corrections: the swarm's per-subdirectory spawning mechanism, cargo-install build instructions, and registration-time metadata reporting were removed or re-scoped to what the cited slices actually state. Evidence coverage: 198 of 293 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
